    {
      "id": "t1",
      "instruction": "Concrete frame with reversed tip lateral forces\n\nReconstruct the structure from the attached dimensioned drawings and, where supplied, DXF. Use the matching member labels in the property, assignment and load appendices. Geometry and support evidence must be read from the drawings. Perform first-order linear elastic analysis using OpenSees; save the self-weight OFF and no-rigid-diaphragm settings. Use explicit section/material stiffness and signed right-handed global axes, Z upward. Retain actual load positions and distributed loads.\n\nReport all of the following for each stated selection, with signs and units:\n- D: free tip ux [combination-D-tip-ux]\n- D: free tip uz [combination-D-tip-uz]\n- D: right base column at bottom M2 [combination-D-c1-1-i-M2]\n- D+W+: free tip ux [combination-D+W+-tip-ux]\n- D+W+: free tip uz [combination-D+W+-tip-uz]\n- D+W+: right base column at bottom M2 [combination-D+W+-c1-1-i-M2]\n- D+W-: free tip ux [combination-D+W--tip-ux]\n- D+W-: free tip uz [combination-D+W--tip-uz]\n- D+W-: right base column at bottom M2 [combination-D+W--c1-1-i-M2]\n\nProvide labelled model and result figures consistent with the numerical values. Preserve the input-to-model ID mapping, engine version/settings, current execution log, original result tables and figure data. If an essential datum is missing, ask specifically for it before analysis.\n",
      "state": 1,
      "expectation": "analyze",
